# A Declare array-size digit string that overflows even `long`
# (GMANInlineParse::is_int must reject it, not saturate and accept a
# garbage quantity that later sizes a `new RtFloat[]` in
# GMANParameterList's constructor). gman is expected to fail cleanly on
# the Declare itself, not crash sizing the Surface parameter that follows.
#
# A trailing Sphere follows AGENTS.md's "RIB authoring" section, "The
# desync convention."
Declare "hugearray" "constant float[99999999999999999999]"
Display "malformed_out.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 200 200 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.6]
Surface "plastic" "hugearray" [1.0]
Sphere 0.5 -0.5 0.5 360
WorldEnd
